# Third-party checkouts — reconstructed from .repos, never committed.
# Keep the notes that record our deviations from upstream.
#
# vendor/ holds NESTED GIT CLONES. Do NOT un-ignore the component directories: git would
# record each as a gitlink ("warning: adding embedded git repository"), producing broken
# submodule references with no .gitmodules. Reconstruct them with `vcs import vendor < .repos`.
#
# Vendoring notes therefore live in docs/vendor/<component>.md, NOT inside the clones — a
# file inside a nested repo is owned by that repo and can never be committed here.
vendor/*
!vendor/README.md

# colcon
build/
install/
log/

# Recorded flight data — these belong on the 7 TB external drive, not in git.
# RGB-D at 640x480@30Hz is tens of GB/hour.
#
# EVERY bag format and sidecar, not just the two this project happens to write. Verified
# 2026-08-04 against a real recording (out/park-tour-<stamp>/ holds metadata.yaml +
# <name>_0.mcap) and by probing each form:
#   *.mcap        rosbag2 default storage here
#   *.db3         rosbag2 sqlite3 storage
#   *.db3-shm/-wal/-journal   sqlite sidecars — left behind by an INTERRUPTED recording,
#                 which is exactly when nobody is thinking about `git add`
#   *.active      rosbag2 marks the in-progress split with this suffix
#   *.bag         ROS 1. Nothing here writes one, but an imported dataset would.
# The bag DIRECTORY is covered too: its metadata.yaml and rosbag2_*/ are ignored below.
*.mcap
*.db3
*.db3-shm
*.db3-wal
*.db3-journal
*.active
*.bag
rosbags/

# Large simulator assets — external drive, referenced by path
*.usd
*.usda
*.usdc
sim/ue5/**/Binaries/
sim/ue5/**/Intermediate/
sim/ue5/**/DerivedDataCache/
sim/ue5/**/Saved/

# Model weights — /home/deck/Developments/models or the external drive
*.gguf
*.safetensors

# Tooling
*.AppImage

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets — never committed (.ai/AGENTS.md:465)
*.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
# compose + demo run artifacts (root-anchored so it cannot swallow e.g. ros2_ws/src/*/out)
# No trailing slash: this is a SYMLINK to the external drive, not a directory
# (run artifacts are bulk data and must not live under ~ — see .ai/AGENTS.md). A trailing
# slash matches directories only, so `/out/` would leave the symlink itself untracked-and-shown.
/out

# Claude Code local settings — PERSONAL, not shared. `.claude/` is otherwise untracked and
# would be swept up by `git add -A`; a permission allow-list is a per-operator choice and
# must not ship to anyone cloning this repo.
.claude/settings.local.json

# User-supplied Unreal worlds (SIM-11 bring-your-own-world). Multi-GB project zips and their
# extracted trees. Root-anchored so it cannot swallow e.g. ros2_ws/src/*/assets.
# NOT optional: a 3.5 GB City Park zip landed here untracked, and this repo uses `git add -A`
# routinely — one commit would have tried to stage it.
/assets/

# Run-time settings.json generated by sim_up.sh --spawn (see SIM-13). Per-run and per-world,
# never committed; the reviewed artifact is sim/ue5/settings.json itself.
sim/ue5/.settings.run.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TYPE-BASED BACKSTOP for run artifacts.
#
# Everything above is LOCATION-based — /out, /assets, sim/ue5/**/Saved. That is the right
# first line of defence, but it holds only while every tool keeps writing where it is
# supposed to. `run_scenario.py --outdir .`, a render written next to the script, or a
# rosbag2 default directory in the repo root all escape it — and this repo uses `git add -A`
# routinely. Measured 2026-08-04: 9.5 GB on disk against 3.1 MB tracked, with the entire
# margin protected by convention alone. One mistyped flag stages a 3 GB bag.
#
# So run artifacts are also ignored BY TYPE, wherever they land. Exactly one binary file is
# tracked in this repo, and it is un-ignored explicitly below.

# Video and stills — the render/record path (record_flight.py, render_run_video.py,
# render_combined_video.py, encode_h264.sh) and the capture harness (capture_*.py).
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
# The one deliberate exception: evidence images embedded in worklog renders.
!docs/worklog/assets/**

# rosbag2 output. The bag itself is caught by *.mcap above; these are the sidecar and the
# default directory name, neither of which carries a distinguishing extension.
rosbag2_*/
**/metadata.yaml

# Unreal project trees. The sim/ue5/** rules above only cover a project placed under
# sim/ue5/ — but a bring-your-own-world project can be dropped anywhere, and
# inject_airsim.py writes into whatever tree it is handed.
*.uasset
*.umap
*.pak
*.ubulk
*.uexp
Binaries/
Intermediate/
DerivedDataCache/
Saved/

# World and asset archives landing outside /assets/.
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar
*.gz
*.tgz

# pytest writes .pytest_cache/.gitignore containing `*`, so this is normally invisible — but
# that is pytest's guarantee, not ours, and it vanishes if the directory is created by
# anything else.
.pytest_cache/
